+## The refusal-text test
+
+`representation_refusals.rs` scans every string literal (comments, char literals and raw strings
+recognised, `\` continuations joined) in non-test `.rs` files under `crates/*/src` for the phrases
+"did not build", "does not keep", "is no longer live", and "is value-based". It fails on a literal
+not on `ALLOWED`, and on an `ALLOWED` row that no longer matches anything, so each later task must
+delete its rows. A third test pins the scanner on comments, char literals, raw strings and
+continuations.
+
+The fourth phrase is mine: without it the objectName= refusal, reworded, would match nothing, and
+the spec's criterion says the allow-list holds it. Derivation command (in the doc comment), output
+checked against the rows, comment lines removed:
+
+```
+grep -rnE --include=*.rs 'did not build|does not keep|is no longer live|is value-based' \
+    crates/*/src | grep -vE '/tests(\.rs:|/)'
+```
+
+Owners:
